        "round_cost_follows_declared_panel": "The zero-fill validation issues part of the declared panel with a zero source size, exactly as a cuBLAS staged GEMM does for operand rows outside a logical M smaller than its tile. Removing two thirds of a 24-KiB panel's fetched bytes changes the L2-resident round service by 0.2 percent on both devices, and removing all of them by about 12 percent. A ring round therefore costs its declared panel rather than the bytes it moves.",
        "selection_rule": "Per (declared panel, grid) retain the minimum conservative per-tier round service and the minimum finite intercept across the two idle devices. Each device's per-tier value follows the accepted finite-stream methodology: the intercept runs through the 128- and 512-round completions and the retained service is the smallest residual per round over the measured round domain. Only topologies whose every measured cell stayed inside a ten percent trial spread on both devices are published; the rest are recorded as excluded in the captures.",
